 Retained project specification, public interfaces and supporting implementation establish the component context; the public behavioral clarification pins edge cases used for formal comparison.\nBehavioral clarification: Use declared defaults, including four requesters and the supplied ID masks; asynchronous active-low aresetn and synchronous active-high srst. The retained round-robin module supplies arch_grant from i_arvalid. Its enable is (any i_arvalid AND o_arready) OR a registered grant-empty flag; that flag resets0 and otherwise captures whether old grant is zero. i_arready is grant masked by downstream ready. o_arvalid and o_arch select the granted input, zero for no grant. For each response lane, target when (lane mask AND low AXI_ID_W bits of o_rch) equals the lane mask; i_rvalid/i_rlast gate the downstream inputs by that predicate. Masks can overlap, including the zero mask matching every ID: preserve multiple targeted lanes. o_rready selects the highest-index targeted lane readiness, zero if none; i_rch always forwards o_rch. Do not replace the bitmask predicate with equality or force one-hot response targets. Supporting round-robin modules and the rest of the project remain visible.\n\nOnly the named module definitions in rtl/axicb_mst_switch_rd.sv are collected. All other code is restored from fixed context, including sibling modules. No new output files or unrelated edits affect scoring. You may compile, simulate, and write your own local tests. Hidden reference RTL and equivalence results are unavailable during generation.\n\nFormal contract:\n- axicb_mst_switch_rd: SEC, clock aclk, reset expression !aresetn; default parameter configuration. No additional handshake restrictions.\n\nFollow this completion instruction; PARENT_CONTEXT.md describes the original parent generation task. Save completed RTL at the declared project path.\n</pre></details></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/a9ec46963f6071a5ce0243e811df8e704644e61766f4eb4939